\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {S2.1}{\ignorespaces Within-patient structure in simulated data without a disease signal ($N=200$ patients, 20 features, 20 replicates per cell). AUC difference in pp (with minus without adjustment, points for means and bars for $\pm $1.96 SE) by the latent intraclass correlation (ICC) of the windows, for three marginal distributions (columns) and 10, 50, and 200 windows per patient (rows). A: adjustment before window-level classification (window-level random forest); C: aggregation to patient means before adjustment (patient-level random forest); LR: patient-level logistic regression. Arm B equals A (constant number of windows per patient). Dashed line: zero. AUC, area under the receiver operating characteristic curve; pp, percentage points; SE, standard error.\relax }}{18}{figure.caption.24}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:struktur}{{S2.1}{18}{Within-patient structure in simulated data without a disease signal ($N=200$ patients, 20 features, 20 replicates per cell). AUC difference in pp (with minus without adjustment, points for means and bars for $\pm $1.96 SE) by the latent intraclass correlation (ICC) of the windows, for three marginal distributions (columns) and 10, 50, and 200 windows per patient (rows). A: adjustment before window-level classification (window-level random forest); C: aggregation to patient means before adjustment (patient-level random forest); LR: patient-level logistic regression. Arm B equals A (constant number of windows per patient). Dashed line: zero. AUC, area under the receiver operating characteristic curve; pp, percentage points; SE, standard error.\relax }{figure.caption.24}{}}
